# Wiki travels with commits

Any change that will be committed in this repository must also update the GitHub wiki checkout at `wiki/`.

`wiki/` is a separate git repository (the GitHub wiki). After editing its pages:

1. Commit the page files in this repository as well, so the change is reviewable with the code.
2. Commit inside `wiki/` and push that wiki repository to its GitHub remote.

When the human says "исправь вики" or "fix the wiki", edit this GitHub wiki. That phrase does not mean in-package documentation such as `src/**/contract.md` or the README.

The main tool repository is not pushed unless the human asks. The wiki repository may be pushed as soon as its pages change.
